Random Number Generation
------------------------

To generate random numbers in C, we use the functions rand() and srand(). 

1. rand() 

	* rand() returns a pseudo-random integer
	* The value is in the range 0 to RAND_MAX
	* RAND_MAX is a constant defined in <stdlib.h>

2. srand() 

	* srand() is used to initialize the random number generator
	* it sets the seed value for generating a new sequence of pseudo-random numbers
	* if srand() is not used, rand() produces the same sequence every time the program runs

3. Default behaviour 

	* If srand() is not called, the random number generator behaves as if srand(1) was called. 
	* This means rand() will generate the same sequence of numbers every time the program runs. 

4. Common practice 

	* srand() is usually called once at the start of the program 
	* time(NULL) is commonly used as the seed value to get different results on each run



